## laptop · key differs from the pin · upsert → ✋, source not declared
rc=1
   ✋ ConstraintError: key fingerprint mismatch — <fixture>/tmp/tailscale.gpg
      expected exactly these primary key(s):
        2596A99EAAB33821893C0A79458CA832957F5868
      received:
        00000000000000000000000000000000DEADBEEF
      ⇒ do NOT install this key. it is the trust anchor for every
        package apt will take from that source, so a wrong key here is
        not one bad install — it is every future one, each with a clean
        signature check against the wrong anchor
      ⇒ an EXTRA key is as bad as a wrong one: the pin is a set, so a
        keyring holding the right key plus another still fails, and
        that is deliberate
      ⇒ if upstream genuinely rotated, source the new fingerprint from
        their published documentation — never from the download you are
        trying to verify
      ⇒ tailscale is NOT installed, and its source is NOT declared. a box
        with no tailscale beats a box whose apt trusts an unvouched anchor
      ⇒ the pin's source: keyserver.ubuntu.com, uid info@tailscale.com.
        a real rotation is confirmed from two channels before the pin moves
writes: web_fetch

## laptop · daemon state unread · upsert → 💥, never 'up'
